<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="095" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Document ↔ record multi-association via an intersection entity (owner chose option b, NOT native N:N)</title>
    <phase>0c Secure Documents — upload path decomposition</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Introduces a schema surface and touches the access model's ancestor assumption. Getting the regarding shape wrong is expensive to undo once rows exist.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The load-bearing decisions (polymorphic target list; whether a link confers access) are architectural and interact with the evaluator.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>Schema + access-model interaction; a wrong default on "does a link confer access" is a silent disclosure.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches the access-ancestor model.</parallel-reason>
    <deps></deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, dataverse, schema</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
    <origin>notes/plan-upload-path-decomposition-2026-08-31.md §3. Owner chose option (b), an intersection entity, from live metadata screenshots 2026-08-31.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>One document can belong to only one matter today. The owner wants a document associable to several records — via an INTERSECTION ENTITY, explicitly not native N:N.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE backend engineer with Dataverse schema authority.</role>

  <goal>A document can be associated to multiple records without multiplying `sprk_document` rows and without making the access ancestor multi-valued.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>**Live metadata (owner screenshots, 2026-08-31)**: Document→Matter has **two**
Many-to-one relationships (`sprk_matter_document`, `sprk_sprk_matter_sprk_document_sprk_relatedmatter`);
Document→Project likewise (`sprk_Project_Document_1n`, `…_sprk_relatedproject`); Document→WorkAssignment
has **one** (`sprk_WorkAssignment_Document_1n`). All **Many-to-one** — i.e. *two slots per type*, not a
many-to-many.

**Why NOT native N:N** (all three reasons, do not re-litigate):
  1. It breaks this project's access model — documents inherit **1 hop via a denormalized core
     ancestor**, and N:N makes "the ancestor" multi-valued.
  2. Dataverse intersect tables **cannot carry columns** (no why/who/when/primary-flag) and cannot be
     secured.
  3. The codebase already has the polymorphic-regarding pattern (`sprk_todo` / ADR-024;
     `sprk_event.sprk_regardingrecordid`) — extend that, do not invent a third shape.

🔴 **Two decisions belong IN this task, not before it:**
  - the polymorphic TARGET LIST, and
  - **whether a link confers access. DEFAULT: NO** — the primary lookup stays the access ancestor, so
    the evaluator is untouched. Changing this default is a security decision needing explicit owner
    sign-off, because a link that confers access is a grant path that bypasses the ancestor model.

⚠️ **Do NOT relax the alternate key on the SPE item id** to allow duplicate rows. A second
`sprk_document` row for the same file is the naive workaround and it violates that key — which is
exactly what produces the owner's HTTP 412. Compose's transient-key dedup AND promote-idempotency both
rest on that key.

⚠️ Related context from item 7 (2026-09-03): `sprk_document` has real lookup columns for matter /
project / invoice / workassignment / event — but **NOT** for `sprk_todo`, `account` or `contact`. If
the target list is meant to include any of those, the intersection entity is the mechanism that makes
it possible without adding five more lookup columns. That is an argument FOR this task's shape; state
it in the design rather than adding lookups piecemeal.</background>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/plan-upload-path-decomposition-2026-08-31.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/</file>
      <file>src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Re-verify the live relationship metadata — do not inherit the screenshot summary.</step>
    <step order="1">Decide and RECORD the polymorphic target list, with the reason each target is in or out.</step>
    <step order="2">Decide and RECORD whether a link confers access. Default NO. If YES is proposed, escalate for explicit owner sign-off before any code.</step>
    <step order="3">Design the intersection entity following the ADR-024 regarding pattern; state which columns it carries and why (why/who/when/primary-flag are the point of choosing it over N:N).</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm the evaluator is untouched under the default, by test.</step>
    <step order="5">Confirm the SPE-item-id alternate key is unchanged and Compose's dedup + promote-idempotency still hold.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the design needs a link to confer access, STOP and escalate — that is a grant path outside the ancestor model and needs explicit owner sign-off (root CLAUDE.md §6).</trigger>
    <trigger>If anything appears to require relaxing the SPE-item-id alternate key, STOP — that key is load-bearing for Compose.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>ADR-024's polymorphic regarding pattern (`sprk_todo`, `sprk_event.sprk_regardingrecordid`) already solves "one row, many possible parents".</existing>
    <extension>Extends that established pattern to documents rather than inventing a third association shape. Native N:N was evaluated and rejected for three concrete reasons.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A document that genuinely belongs to two matters can only be represented by a second `sprk_document` row, which violates the SPE-item-id alternate key and surfaces to the user as an HTTP 412 with unsubstituted Dataverse placeholders. Users cannot file a document to more than one record at all.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="schema">Intersection entity for document ↔ record association</output>
    <output type="doc">Recorded decisions: target list, and whether a link confers access</output>
    <output type="test">Evaluator unchanged under the default; alternate key intact</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>A document can be associated to multiple records without a second `sprk_document` row.</criterion>
    <criterion>The SPE-item-id alternate key is unchanged; Compose transient-key dedup and promote-idempotency still pass.</criterion>
    <criterion>Under the default, a link confers NO access — asserted by an evaluator test, not by inspection.</criterion>
    <criterion>The polymorphic target list and the access decision are both recorded with reasons.</criterion>
    <criterion>No native N:N was introduced.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>NOT STARTED. Gates 094's "Use existing" option.</notes>
</task>
